  "term": "existentialism",
  "definition": "Existentialism is a philosophy that examines a person’s existence in the world and argues that human life cannot be fully explained in purely scientific terms. It emphasizes individual freedom and responsibility, along with the personal meaning of ethical, religious, and subjective experiences such as anxiety, guilt, and suffering.",
